- op: discuss  # 83b1
  at: '2026-11-13T22:18:36Z'  # 83b1
  by: agent  # 83b1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 83b1
  clock: 3  # 83b1
  nonce: 83b1  # 83b1
  message: "Done in PR #2176 (commits e12a740bb4 and aa5631fe0f).\nRULE: a listing is cut by what its entries cost. Source Files takes entries in rank order until the next would pass its ADR-0005 share (never fewer than five); the count is no longer the share over 12 tokens. The closing line of a cut listing says how many files were left out, how many of them are tests, and the top-level directories that hold them. Past the files worth naming one by one the listing stops at its share and summarises; there is no second cut-off by score (ADR-0005 says why: the share bounds the list, and a score threshold would need a value nobody has measured).\nTHE SAME MECHANISM IN TWO MORE PLACES, fixed in the second commit: Key Symbols (share over 35 tokens a symbol) and the Additional Files listing (share over 12 tokens a path). A section that passes its share pushes the sketch over budget, and the last step of generation drops whole sections from the end. On dev before this work: killbill at 8k without source had no Key Symbols, kserve at 32k without source no Additional Files, this repository at 8k without source ended at Source Files. Source Files Content now also takes its shares over the first N files (ADR-0005's \"effective N\", which the code had never done), so a small --with-source budget prints source instead of an empty section.\nSOURCE FILES AS A SHARE OF THE SKETCH, before -> after, with entries (tests among them). The ADR share is 10% of what is left of the budget with --with-source, 25% without.\n  this repository   8k  with 14.8% (36) -> 5.7% (13)        without 42.6% (87) -> 12.6% (32)\n                    32k with 23.9% (233) -> 8.9% (87)       without 55.6% (431) -> 16.1% (158)\n                    128k with 26.0% (1033, 556 tests) -> 9.7% (372, 0 tests)   without 49.5% (1935, 1456 tests) -> 25.1% (911, 434 tests)\n  killbill (Java)   8k  with 12.9% (45) -> 7.1% (25)        without 36.9% (104) -> 15.6% (56)\n                    32k with 17.0% (245) -> 9.3% (132)      without 31.1% (454) -> 17.0% (248)\n                    128k with 18.1% (1045) -> 9.8% (570)    without 36.0% (1740) -> 26.4% (1294)\n  kserve            8k  with 7.5% (42) -> 6.5% (38)         without 18.4% (101) -> 15.0% (81)\n                    32k with 11.4% (240) -> 9.1% (193)      without 27.4% (499) -> 18.7% (388)\n                    128k with 11.2% (971) -> 9.8% (837)     without 17.1% -> 16.6% (all 971)\n  alertmanager (Go, bare paths)  8k with 4.6% (51) -> 8.1% (91); without 11.6% (127) -> 19.0% (193); 32k with 6.3% (251) -> 7.9% (all 312)\n  prometheus (Go, bare paths)    8k with 4.8% (51) -> 8.5% (77); without 13.7% (123) -> 18.5% (167); 32k with 7.4% (251) -> 9.6% (316)\nMeasured against what is left of the budget when the section is reached (estimated from the text before it): before, 17 of the 30 sketches had Source Files more than 15% over its share (this repository 26.8-69.4% where the share is 10 or 25%); after, 3, all at 8k (kserve 11.7% with source, killbill 13.8% with and 34.0% without). I have not traced those three; my reading, not verified, is that the Structure tree is rewritten after the share is computed, so the share was taken from a larger remainder. Every sketch is within its total budget. Both directions in the table are the rule: long paths and docstrings get fewer entries, bare short paths more.\nThe filed instance, this repository at 128k with source: the closing line now reads \"- ... and 1563 more files (1457 of them tests): `packages/` 1373, `tests/` 172, `scripts/` 13, 5 elsewhere\".\nSECTIONS, same 30 sketches: none lost a section; eight gained one. Without source: killbill 8k, this repository 8k and 32k gained Key Symbols and Additional Files (this repository at 32k went 25,722 -> 31,977 tokens of 32,000); kserve 32k gained Additional Files. With source at 8k: kserve, killbill, prometheus and this repository gained Source Files Content (0 -> 1,888 / 1,888 / 2,250 / 1,217 tokens), alertmanager's went 415 -> 2,825. Every sketch is within its budget.\nA COST OF THE SOURCE-CONTENT CHANGE: with source, Source Files Content now uses its 75% share, so Additional Files Content gets less than it used to take by default (this repository at 32k: 13,021 -> 5,551 tokens of documents, 1,217 -> 12,675 of source).\nWHAT THE REVIEW GOT WRONG, for the record: the test files were not listed alphabetically; they are in rank order.\nMutations: 9 on the first commit, 10 on the second, each turning a test red. Two of them passed every existing test until a test was written: the Source Files in-degree statistic was asserted only to be >= 0, and the Additional Files statistic was not pinned at all.\nNOT DONE, to be filed: without source content a sketch still under-fills a large budget when its sections run out of entries (alertmanager at 128k uses 17% of the budget, before and after); Entry Points and Data Models are still sized by a count (they take a third and a fifth of what is left, so passing their share shrinks later sections and cannot push the sketch over)."  # 83b1
